but I know it's been a trip,

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:33.660
but I had prided myself-

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.580
- As a viewer I feel sorry for you.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:36.741
- Oh, do you? Yeah, well-
- Yeah.

00:06:36.741 --> 00:06:38.467
- Even when you're kind of a jerk,

00:06:38.467 --> 00:06:39.600
I just feel sorry for you.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:40.740
- I'll take it, I'll take it.
- Yeah.

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:42.138
- I need it for the healing.

00:06:42.138 --> 00:06:42.971
(laughing)

00:06:42.971 --> 00:06:45.570
It's tough, you know, like
I used to pride myself

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:46.770
on letting it go before I went home.

00:06:46.770 --> 00:06:48.390
But this one, by season 2 or 3,

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:49.860
my wife was like, "You are different.

00:06:49.860 --> 00:06:51.240
What's happening?"
- Yeah.

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.710
- And so I was carrying him home

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:54.240
and basically now he has the floor

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:55.650
and Wes is kind of off in the back

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:57.240
waiting for his moment again.

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:59.130
- Dude, yeah. It's an intense role.

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:00.540
And even like you'd said, "The Godfather,"

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.640
even the dynamic of family in it

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:05.160
is really hardcore.
- Yeah.

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:06.000
- Very tough.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.170
Scenes with Beth are tough, you know,

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:09.060
and she, it's a hard thing to get through,

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:10.530
but we trust each other.
- Beth!

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:11.767
- That's how we do it, but yeah...

00:07:11.767 --> 00:07:14.827
- Sheez, Beth, I'm just like,
(laughing)

00:07:14.827 --> 00:07:16.320
"It's a whole ep...

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:18.030
Just a whole show in itself."

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:19.510
I'm just like, "There's a lot in there."

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:20.343
(laughing)

00:07:20.343 --> 00:07:21.176
Yeah, that character.

00:07:21.176 --> 00:07:22.417
I'm just like, "What are
these writers doing?"

00:07:22.417 --> 00:07:23.670
- Oh, yeah.
- Oh, man.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:24.957
Anyway, it's so good though.

00:07:24.957 --> 00:07:27.120
So, were either of you
comfortable on horses

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:28.770
or were you those actors that totally lied

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:30.570
and said, "I can ride
a horse" and couldn't?

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:31.710
- I think it was on my resume

00:07:31.710 --> 00:07:32.550
that I could ride a horse,

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:33.749
but I was totally lying.
- No, but that doesn't mean

00:07:33.749 --> 00:07:34.647
it's real. Okay.
- No, I was terrified.

00:07:34.647 --> 00:07:35.480
(laughing)

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:36.413
Not at all.
- Yeah.

00:07:36.413 --> 00:07:37.246
- I was terrible.

00:07:37.246 --> 00:07:38.850
- You look like you can ride a horse.

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:39.840
- I can a little bit, now.

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:40.673
You know, we've been working
- Yeah.

00:07:40.673 --> 00:07:42.510
on it for 5 years at this point.

00:07:42.510 --> 00:07:43.343
- Yeah.
- You know,

00:07:43.343 --> 00:07:45.180
they've had us doing a lot of, you know,

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:46.260
working with some really good people,

00:07:46.260 --> 00:07:47.400
doing some cowboy camps,

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.233
that sort of thing.
- Yeah.

00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:49.440
- So, yeah a little better now.

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:52.050
- Wait is cowboy camp,
like "City slickers?"

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:53.220
I imagine that's what it is.

00:07:53.220 --> 00:07:54.480
Like, you know-
- Yeah.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:55.560
- Pretty much.
- But with actors.

00:07:55.560 --> 00:07:57.210
Like really annoying actors.
- That's insane.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:58.043
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:07:58.043 --> 00:07:58.876
- Yeah, they were like,

00:07:58.876 --> 00:07:59.709
we went on this cowboy camp

00:07:59.709 --> 00:08:01.290
that we had these like, Paul Bunyan type,

00:08:01.290 --> 00:08:03.240
real cowboys who do pack rides.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:04.073
- Yeah.

00:08:04.073 --> 00:08:04.906
- And like we wanted,

00:08:04.906 --> 00:08:06.180
we were to go out in the, off the grid,

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:08.670
and live with them and try to survive.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:09.940
And learn how to ride horses and stuff.

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:10.773
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:08:10.773 --> 00:08:11.640
- But it was an adventure though.

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:12.930
- Wait, that sounds fun!

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:13.763
- It was crazy though.

00:08:13.763 --> 00:08:16.680
We kinda got separated from
those Paul Bunyan types

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:19.812
and it was just actors alone
in the woods for a minute.

00:08:19.812 --> 00:08:20.645
(laughing)
For a minute.

00:08:20.645 --> 00:08:21.562
- How do you get, how
does one get separated?

00:08:21.562 --> 00:08:22.395
Were they just playing a prank on you

00:08:22.395 --> 00:08:23.520
and they leave you? Like what?

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:24.570
- We were wondering if it was

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.099
like part of the thing,
- Yeah.

00:08:26.099 --> 00:08:27.150
- like, "They're doing this on purpose.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:27.983
They'll be here any minute."
- Yeah.

00:08:27.983 --> 00:08:29.760
No, too late.
- No, we didn't see 'em

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:30.593
'til the next day.

00:08:30.593 --> 00:08:32.040
We were just-
- And you're in Montana?

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:33.150
- Utah at that moment.
- Yeah.

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:33.983
- Oh, I was like,
- Yeah, yeah.

00:08:33.983 --> 00:08:35.760
"Were there bears and wolves?"
- Yeah.

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:36.593
Were there bears there too?

00:08:36.593 --> 00:08:37.426
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:08:37.426 --> 00:08:38.880
I'm like, "On my property alone

00:08:38.880 --> 00:08:39.713
all of that exists."

00:08:39.713 --> 00:08:40.590
- We thought-
We thought we saw a bear

00:08:40.590 --> 00:08:41.760
in the distance. You remember that?

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:43.320
We were like, "There's
some figure way off"

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:45.448
and we couldn't figure
out what exactly it was.

00:08:45.448 --> 00:08:46.560
- Yeah, I think it was one of the cowboys

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:47.634
keeping an eye on us.
(laughing)

00:08:47.634 --> 00:08:48.467
(indistinct)

00:08:48.467 --> 00:08:49.300
- Just messing with you,
- Yeah.

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.133
- dressed up
- Yeah.

00:08:50.133 --> 00:08:50.966
as Smokey the bear.
- Just making sure

00:08:50.966 --> 00:08:52.590
we didn't die.
(laughing)

00:08:52.590 --> 00:08:54.120
- Did you ever ride horses before,

00:08:54.120 --> 00:08:54.953
or did you...

00:08:54.953 --> 00:08:55.786
- I did the same thing.

00:08:55.786 --> 00:08:57.060
I put it on my resume and I actually,

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:59.700
I got really close to a job, "Beloved,"

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:00.930
this movie by Jonathan Demme

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:03.810
and they put me on a
train out to Philadelphia

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:05.760
from New York to meet
him to get this role.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:06.752
Small role,
- Yeah.

00:09:06.752 --> 00:09:07.710
but it is important to me.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:10.050
And I went and met with him
and we walked the hallway

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:12.450
and he was sort of like,
"Can you do an accent?"

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:13.560
I'm like, "Yeah, I can do accents."

00:09:13.560 --> 00:09:15.000
He says, "Can you ride a horse?"

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.980
I said, "Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah,

00:09:16.980 --> 00:09:18.300
I wrote it on my resume,
- Total!

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:19.140
- right? Yeah."

00:09:19.140 --> 00:09:20.005
- I can also lie.
- Then he said,

00:09:20.005 --> 00:09:21.192
"Well you need to go over there."

00:09:21.192 --> 00:09:22.088
Yeah. (laughing)

00:09:22.088 --> 00:09:23.490
- Do you need me to do that?
- Yeah.

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:24.570
- He said, "Why don't you go over there

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:26.010
to the wranglers and ride some horses

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:26.940
and they'll see where you're at."

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:28.257
And I just panicked
- Oh.

00:09:28.257 --> 00:09:29.760
- and I got on and as soon as I got on,

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:31.184
they I was lying.

00:09:31.184 --> 00:09:32.670
(all laughing)

00:09:32.670 --> 00:09:33.779
I got the role.

00:09:33.779 --> 00:09:34.612
- He did.
(laughing)

00:09:34.612 --> 00:09:35.445
- Yeah.
- There you go.

00:09:35.445 --> 00:09:36.278
- Lying works.

00:09:36.278 --> 00:09:37.410
- They were like, "He's bold, check."

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:38.243
- Yeah.

00:09:38.243 --> 00:09:39.076
- He's like, "He'll do anything."

00:09:39.076 --> 00:09:40.258
- I guess so.

00:09:40.258 --> 00:09:41.178
- That is frightening,

00:09:41.178 --> 00:09:42.011
That you just,
- It is frightening.

00:09:42.011 --> 00:09:43.491
- they're like, "Hop on a horse and go."

00:09:43.491 --> 00:09:44.324
- (indistinct) horses, yeah.
- Yeah.

00:09:44.324 --> 00:09:45.157
- Soon as you touch 'em,
they're like, "Dang,"

00:09:45.157 --> 00:09:45.990
they took off, yeah.

00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:46.890
- Yeah, they sense fear.

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:48.510
Don't be fearful.

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:50.280
Are your kids into the show?

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:52.050
- Oh yeah, I mean, they
don't watch it, but-

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:53.127
- They know a bi-atch.

00:09:53.127 --> 00:09:53.960
(all laughing)

00:09:53.960 --> 00:09:55.163
Just Beth alone.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:09:55.163 --> 00:09:57.030
They do know there's some bad things

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:58.230
that are right to do.

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:59.700
One's not watch Yellowstone yet,

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:02.040
but no, they wanted to ride horses

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:02.910
at first and they did.

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:04.020
And then we went back and forth.

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:05.550
But what my son was really up to

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:07.080
in the first couple seasons was

00:10:07.080 --> 00:10:09.240
he was trying to land Luke Grimes.

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:11.280
Attached to his little script he wrote,

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:12.113
remember?
- Oh, yeah.

00:10:12.113 --> 00:10:13.560
- The character's name.
- What was mine?

00:10:13.560 --> 00:10:14.840
- Jake Microsoft.
- Jake Microsoft.

00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:16.860
(all laughing)

00:10:16.860 --> 00:10:18.439
- My son was 6 or 7, yeah.

00:10:18.439 --> 00:10:19.663
- I gotta stop laughing.

00:10:19.663 --> 00:10:20.496
- He spent a lot of energy
- I forgot about.

00:10:20.496 --> 00:10:21.691
- trying to bug Luke.

00:10:21.691 --> 00:10:22.524
(laughing)

00:10:22.524 --> 00:10:23.357
Not me.

00:10:23.357 --> 00:10:24.190
(laughing)

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:25.023
- Not you.

00:10:25.023 --> 00:10:25.856
(laughing)

00:10:25.856 --> 00:10:26.689
He wanted a real...

00:10:26.689 --> 00:10:28.110
Isn't that amazing how humbling it is?

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:28.943
Your kids?

00:10:28.943 --> 00:10:29.776
- Oh, he didn't care for whatever I did.

00:10:29.776 --> 00:10:31.500
- Oh no, literally, like my kids said

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:32.333
they didn't care at all.

00:10:32.333 --> 00:10:33.166
And literally, I came home

00:10:33.166 --> 00:10:34.680
and like Ariana Grande
was on "The Voice" with me

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:36.240
and they were like, "Who?"

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:38.247
And I was like, "What?"
- Yeah, oh yeah.

00:10:38.247 --> 00:10:39.533
- I was like, "They
don't care what you do."

00:10:39.533 --> 00:10:40.366
- No.

